# The boreutils tree M-PX3 runs (px12; tools/mkboreutils builds it).
#
# boreutils trunk at the time of px12 (2026-10-07): 2f15585, pinned in
# its own wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf 0.2.23 / lupin 0.1.46 / wolf-std
# 6a0df5e. tools/mkboreutils builds it with THAT toolchain (the archive
# by the digest boreutils names, the std tree at the commit it names),
# not with kernel/wolf.pin's: the binaries are boreutils' own, built
# from boreutils' own tree.
#
# px15 (2026-10-08) moves it to boreutils trunk 50d8907: bu17's pin
# (wolf 0.2.25 / lupin 0.1.48 / wolf-std 0f74ec5) and bu18's `ls`, so
# /bin/ls is boreutils' and busybox leaves the initramfs.
#
# px26 (2026-10-11) moves it to boreutils trunk 870815c (bu20): bu19's
# and bu20's pins (wolf 0.2.27 / lupin 0.1.50, the std the tree names)
# and bu20's `ls -l` and family, `stat`, `readlink` and `env`, which
# join the shell's /bin. Its `cat` copies with `copy_file_range` and
# `sendfile` (bu19), and its long listing reads /etc/passwd,
# /etc/group and /etc/localtime.
#
# px27 (2026-10-11) moves it to boreutils trunk abc59f5 (bu21): the same
# toolchain (wolf 0.2.27 / lupin 0.1.50) and bu21's `mkdir`, `rmdir`,
# `rm`, `mv` and `cp`, 36 utilities in all.
BORE_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/boreutils
BORE_REV=abc59f5bc3ff832aad8bd819017bf6cdae3df9a3
